# SQL's `ORDER BY ... DESC`: the body parses as `sort by`, so `DESC` gets its own DS0105 in the same pass; both fixes apply.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | ORDER BY amount DESC
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..41
  PIPELINE@0..40
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    SORT_OP@20..40
      IDENT@20..25 "ORDER"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      IDENT@26..28 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
      SORT_KEY@29..40
        NAME_REF@29..35
          IDENT@29..35 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
        IDENT@36..40 "DESC"
  WHITESPACE@40..41 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `ORDER BY` is not an operator
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | ORDER BY amount DESC
  |                     ^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: sort rows with `sort by`: `sort by amount desc`

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `DESC` is not a sort direction
  --> query:1:37
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | ORDER BY amount DESC
  |                                     ^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `desc`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc
which parses without errors
